it's sunny it's a nice day you're too.

00:04:56.763 --> 00:05:00.300
And so yes

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:02.702
the paper was

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:07.140
an attempt to

00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:10.109
to device a view of communication

00:05:10.109 --> 00:05:13.646
that could be like a starting point

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:17.483
for ecological and in active approaches

00:05:17.483 --> 00:05:19.452
to language and communication.

00:05:19.452 --> 00:05:22.322
And the problem that we saw

00:05:22.522 --> 00:05:24.657
is that in most

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:29.195
language sciences, like linguistics,

00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:32.031
in the field of language,

00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:33.566
in mainstream philosophy, in language

00:05:33.566 --> 00:05:35.702
and in biology of communication,

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:37.136
most researchers,

00:05:37.136 --> 00:05:40.473
most people end up at IQ automatically

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:42.241
a view of communication

00:05:42.241 --> 00:05:44.243
in which communication is

00:05:44.243 --> 00:05:46.112
essentially transmitting

00:05:47.714 --> 00:05:49.682
information or transmission,

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:50.950
transmitting content

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:53.586
or an idea to another being.

00:05:53.586 --> 00:05:54.387
So

00:05:55.254 --> 00:05:56.322
usually like

00:05:56.322 --> 00:05:57.990
in linguistic communication,

00:05:57.990 --> 00:05:58.624
that would be like,

00:05:58.624 --> 00:05:59.625
I have the belief

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:01.894
that it's a sunny day outside.

00:06:01.894 --> 00:06:04.831
I say it's a sunny day outside.

00:06:04.831 --> 00:06:06.766
And then by doing this,

00:06:06.766 --> 00:06:08.568
I am transmitting to you

00:06:08.568 --> 00:06:09.302
the belief

00:06:09.302 --> 00:06:11.304
that it's a sunny day outside.

00:06:11.304 --> 00:06:12.271
So that's the

00:06:12.271 --> 00:06:14.073
basic view of communication,

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:15.174
the transmission view

00:06:15.174 --> 00:06:16.142
that is

00:06:16.142 --> 00:06:18.411
more or less adopted by everybody

00:06:19.545 --> 00:06:22.248
in in linguistics and in

00:06:22.415 --> 00:06:23.616
cognitive science.

00:06:23.616 --> 00:06:25.418
But a lot of people at least,

00:06:25.418 --> 00:06:27.153
and that's a view of communication

00:06:27.153 --> 00:06:28.755
that is problematic

00:06:28.755 --> 00:06:29.822
from an active

00:06:29.822 --> 00:06:31.791
and ecological perspective

00:06:31.791 --> 00:06:35.194
because it relies on the notion

00:06:35.194 --> 00:06:36.162
of content

00:06:36.162 --> 00:06:38.297
and the notion of representation

00:06:38.297 --> 00:06:40.133
to transmit a content,

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:42.201
I must have a representation in my head

00:06:42.835 --> 00:06:45.204
and then I can transmit it to you

00:06:45.204 --> 00:06:46.439
so that you can entertain

00:06:46.439 --> 00:06:48.274
this representation in your head.

00:06:48.274 --> 00:06:50.743
But as is quite well known

00:06:51.277 --> 00:06:53.346
in active and ecological approaches

00:06:53.346 --> 00:06:54.547
to cognition,

00:06:54.547 --> 00:06:56.983
I reject the notion of representation,

00:06:56.983 --> 00:06:57.383
the notion,

00:06:57.383 --> 00:06:58.551
the notion of content

00:06:58.551 --> 00:07:01.521
as basic building block of cognition.

00:07:01.854 --> 00:07:04.590
So the transmission view is a problem

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:06.959
from an active ecological view.

00:07:06.959 --> 00:07:07.326
And so

00:07:07.326 --> 00:07:08.161
what we tried to do

00:07:08.161 --> 00:07:11.531
was to develop a view of communication

00:07:11.831 --> 00:07:13.466
from which ecological

00:07:13.466 --> 00:07:14.967
and active approaches

00:07:14.967 --> 00:07:18.504
could start to understand language

00:07:18.504 --> 00:07:21.974
and communication without having to rely

00:07:21.974 --> 00:07:23.876
on the notion of content

00:07:23.876 --> 00:07:25.111
or representation.

00:07:25.111 --> 00:07:25.711
So that's like

00:07:25.711 --> 00:07:28.080
the basic motivation of the paper.

00:07:28.281 --> 00:07:30.750
That's what we were trying to do

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:32.552
and we thought that

00:07:33.686 --> 00:07:35.188
active and friends and

00:07:35.188 --> 00:07:36.622
especially its ecology

00:07:36.622 --> 00:07:39.158
interpretation could be useful

00:07:39.625 --> 00:07:41.060
for doing that.

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:42.161
And,

00:07:42.295 --> 00:07:43.196
and yet

00:07:43.196 --> 00:07:45.531
the thing that you mentioned, Bleu.

00:07:45.998 --> 00:07:46.432
Yeah,

00:07:47.333 --> 00:07:49.368
the aim was to devise

00:07:49.368 --> 00:07:50.937
a view of communication

00:07:50.937 --> 00:07:52.472
that could be perfectly general,

00:07:52.472 --> 00:07:54.574
so that could be applied to

00:07:54.574 --> 00:07:55.942
animal communication,

00:07:55.942 --> 00:07:57.543
maybe communication

00:07:57.543 --> 00:07:58.945
between cells at the, at,

00:07:58.945 --> 00:08:00.947
the, at the more,

00:08:00.947 --> 00:08:03.115
at the more small scale level

00:08:03.316 --> 00:08:04.317
and eventually

00:08:04.317 --> 00:08:05.318
maybe communication

00:08:05.318 --> 00:08:06.652
between groups

00:08:06.652 --> 00:08:10.189
at the more at a larger scale so that

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:11.924
the view to

00:08:11.924 --> 00:08:12.425
the attempt

00:08:12.425 --> 00:08:14.927
was to produce a view of communication

00:08:14.927 --> 00:08:16.529
that is perfectly general

00:08:16.529 --> 00:08:19.365
and that can be precise and

00:08:20.433 --> 00:08:21.200
along the way.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:22.768
So that we can, for instance,

00:08:22.768 --> 00:08:25.204
precise the conception of communication

00:08:25.204 --> 00:08:25.972
to apply it

00:08:25.972 --> 00:08:28.140
to cooperative communication,

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:28.708
for instance,

00:08:28.708 --> 00:08:30.510
which is the kind of communication

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:32.712
that is characteristic of human

00:08:32.712 --> 00:08:34.180
communicative interaction,

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:35.882
and that was treated

00:08:35.882 --> 00:08:38.618
notably in the cell paper to which you

00:08:39.151 --> 00:08:40.219
alluded to.

00:08:40.219 --> 00:08:42.755
So that's the aim of the paper.

00:08:42.922 --> 00:08:45.157
And so because of its generality,

00:08:45.391 --> 00:08:47.159
it's the paper that is really

00:08:48.227 --> 00:08:49.896
in a way superficial because

00:08:49.896 --> 00:08:51.230
it's it really treats

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:53.699
a lot of topics really quickly.

00:08:53.699 --> 00:08:54.467
But that was like

00:08:54.467 --> 00:08:55.868
a big road map

00:08:55.868 --> 00:08:58.037
for a view of communication

00:08:58.037 --> 00:08:58.971
that could be used

00:08:58.971 --> 00:09:02.041
by ecological and active researchers.

00:09:02.041 --> 00:09:03.242
So that was essentially

00:09:03.242 --> 00:09:06.078
what we tried to do in this paper.

