avoidance is as the subset

00:43:23.634 --> 00:43:26.036
that is common to both

00:43:26.036 --> 00:43:27.938
individual fields of affordances.

00:43:27.938 --> 00:43:30.307
But I think that neglects this point,

00:43:30.307 --> 00:43:32.042
this autonomy of

00:43:32.042 --> 00:43:33.177
the field of affordances

00:43:33.177 --> 00:43:35.913
that is shared in the interaction.

00:43:35.913 --> 00:43:36.480
I don't know

00:43:36.480 --> 00:43:37.481
if I'm being clear,

00:43:37.481 --> 00:43:39.683
but I define the shared

00:43:39.683 --> 00:43:41.185
field of affordances

00:43:41.185 --> 00:43:44.221
as a product of the combination

00:43:44.221 --> 00:43:45.322
that a combination

00:43:45.322 --> 00:43:46.690
of the two individual

00:43:46.690 --> 00:43:47.791
fields of affordances.

00:43:47.791 --> 00:43:49.994
But it seems that there's

00:43:49.994 --> 00:43:51.061
a lack of autonomy

00:43:51.061 --> 00:43:51.795
in the shell

00:43:51.795 --> 00:43:52.262
field that

00:43:52.262 --> 00:43:56.333
I don't know how to account for.

00:43:56.333 --> 00:43:59.470
FRIEDMAN: That makes me think of the ants case

00:43:59.970 --> 00:44:02.940
where one nest may might be able to

00:44:03.574 --> 00:44:06.210
grab a single seed and carry home.

00:44:06.677 --> 00:44:10.180
So that would be compatible with a view

00:44:10.180 --> 00:44:11.382
on communication

00:44:11.382 --> 00:44:13.050
shaping the field of affordances

00:44:13.050 --> 00:44:14.251
because it modifies

00:44:15.185 --> 00:44:15.853
the capacity

00:44:15.853 --> 00:44:16.720
for another nest

00:44:16.720 --> 00:44:17.855
made to pick up that seed

00:44:17.855 --> 00:44:19.690
because it's been moved

00:44:19.690 --> 00:44:21.091
doesn't need to have any

00:44:21.091 --> 00:44:22.760
representational content,

00:44:22.760 --> 00:44:23.694
although especially when

00:44:23.694 --> 00:44:24.995
we're linguistically describing

00:44:24.995 --> 00:44:25.796
it does so

00:44:25.796 --> 00:44:27.998
definitely want to come back to that.

00:44:28.098 --> 00:44:31.101
Then there's this

00:44:31.101 --> 00:44:32.403
seed grabbing ability

00:44:32.403 --> 00:44:34.171
which is predicated on

00:44:34.171 --> 00:44:35.973
a lower level of audience,

00:44:35.973 --> 00:44:36.740
like the ability

00:44:36.740 --> 00:44:39.977
to grasp with the mandibles.

00:44:39.977 --> 00:44:42.279
And that lower level of audience enables

00:44:42.813 --> 00:44:44.748
true joint action

00:44:44.748 --> 00:44:46.884
like multiple nest mates

00:44:46.884 --> 00:44:47.718
working together

00:44:47.718 --> 00:44:50.154
to drag something bigger home,

00:44:50.154 --> 00:44:51.088
but dragging something

00:44:51.088 --> 00:44:52.623
bigger isn't in the fore,

00:44:52.623 --> 00:44:54.758
and so even exists

00:44:54.758 --> 00:44:56.727
at the single decimate level.

00:44:56.727 --> 00:44:59.096
So there's like shared affordances

00:44:59.096 --> 00:45:00.030
and joint action

00:45:00.030 --> 00:45:03.000
at the level of what we can both do.

00:45:03.867 --> 00:45:04.635
And then

00:45:04.635 --> 00:45:06.503
there's also this very interesting

00:45:06.503 --> 00:45:08.172
higher level view

00:45:08.172 --> 00:45:10.874
where perhaps novel affordances

00:45:11.442 --> 00:45:14.378
become accessible, but then whom

00:45:14.378 --> 00:45:15.145
or to what

00:45:15.145 --> 00:45:19.416
or when do these special affordances or

00:45:20.718 --> 00:45:21.819
maybe nested

00:45:21.819 --> 00:45:24.788
system affordances come into play?

00:45:24.788 --> 00:45:27.991
And how will we mediate the the handoff

00:45:27.991 --> 00:45:28.625
or like the way

00:45:28.625 --> 00:45:29.827
that those different levels

00:45:29.827 --> 00:45:31.228
of affordances

00:45:31.228 --> 00:45:34.865
come into relevance or out of relevance,

00:45:34.865 --> 00:45:38.368
Bleu.

00:45:38.368 --> 00:45:40.571
KNIGHT: So in terms of that modeling,

00:45:40.571 --> 00:45:41.772
the field of affordances

00:45:41.772 --> 00:45:44.408
like it changes through time.

00:45:45.776 --> 00:45:47.177
And this is why I like

00:45:47.177 --> 00:45:48.879
I was thinking about

00:45:48.879 --> 00:45:50.080
a competition

00:45:50.080 --> 00:45:52.382
like in a tug of war between two people.

00:45:53.183 --> 00:45:55.319
Both of them have the appearance to win

00:45:55.352 --> 00:45:57.321
or there could be a tie, right?

00:45:57.321 --> 00:45:59.523
But like it's a potential opportunity

00:45:59.523 --> 00:46:00.424
for either one to win,

00:46:00.424 --> 00:46:02.493
but only one can be the winner.

00:46:02.493 --> 00:46:04.261
And so then one person winning,

00:46:04.261 --> 00:46:06.864
like by default, you know, makes

00:46:06.864 --> 00:46:08.799
it makes the other person lose.

00:46:08.799 --> 00:46:09.500
And so this

00:46:09.500 --> 00:46:10.501
this field

00:46:10.501 --> 00:46:11.769
of avoidance, of thinking through

00:46:11.769 --> 00:46:13.537
time is really interesting

00:46:13.537 --> 00:46:15.672
and I think very broadly applicable

00:46:16.240 --> 00:46:20.544
for modeling all kinds of processes.

00:46:20.544 --> 00:46:21.278
TISON: Yeah, that's true.

00:46:21.278 --> 00:46:23.580
And the idea about

00:46:23.580 --> 00:46:25.048
the collective

00:46:25.048 --> 00:46:25.783
affordances, there's

00:46:25.783 --> 00:46:27.084
been some interesting,

00:46:27.084 --> 00:46:28.519
interesting work on that

00:46:28.519 --> 00:46:31.622
and clearly some organisms like ants

00:46:31.922 --> 00:46:33.991
don't perceive collective affordances.

00:46:33.991 --> 00:46:35.392
They perceive

00:46:35.526 --> 00:46:36.460
is they perceive something,

00:46:36.460 --> 00:46:36.960
they perceive

00:46:36.960 --> 00:46:38.362
their individual affordances

00:46:38.362 --> 00:46:40.364
and collectively level.

00:46:40.364 --> 00:46:43.367
There's the the taking of this

00:46:43.634 --> 00:46:44.368
higher level

00:46:44.368 --> 00:46:46.470
affordances, this collective affordances

00:46:46.470 --> 00:46:47.070
of our dance.

00:46:47.070 --> 00:46:49.473
But they don't perceive individually,

00:46:49.473 --> 00:46:50.107
probably

00:46:50.107 --> 00:46:52.242
I don't think they do perceive

00:46:52.242 --> 00:46:53.811
individually the audience.

00:46:53.811 --> 00:46:56.213
But some organisms such as humans,

00:46:56.446 --> 00:46:58.448
I think because we have

00:46:58.448 --> 00:47:00.684
maybe a deeper generative of something,

00:47:00.684 --> 00:47:02.052
we are able to

00:47:02.052 --> 00:47:03.120
perceive some collective

00:47:03.120 --> 00:47:04.288
affordances because we're

00:47:05.355 --> 00:47:06.356
sensible to them.

00:47:06.356 --> 00:47:07.624
For instance,

00:47:07.624 --> 00:47:09.960
if I'm moving with a friend,

00:47:09.960 --> 00:47:11.295
I can perceive that

00:47:11.295 --> 00:47:12.229
a couch

00:47:12.229 --> 00:47:13.697
is unmovable by me,

00:47:13.697 --> 00:47:16.066
but I can perceive it as movable by us.

00:47:16.066 --> 00:47:17.434
And then I can see like, Oh,

00:47:17.434 --> 00:47:19.203
we could move this couch together

00:47:19.203 --> 00:47:20.204
because I perceive it

00:47:20.204 --> 00:47:23.707
as something that can be acted upon,

00:47:23.907 --> 00:47:26.143
not just by me, but with somebody else.

00:47:26.143 --> 00:47:28.111
And then I have a perception,

00:47:28.111 --> 00:47:29.680
it appears in my individual

00:47:29.680 --> 00:47:30.681
feed of our dance

00:47:30.681 --> 00:47:32.015
as a collective for dance.

00:47:32.015 --> 00:47:34.351
But that's different from the, the,

00:47:34.518 --> 00:47:36.286
the ants who

00:47:36.286 --> 00:47:37.754
achieve a collective action,

00:47:37.754 --> 00:47:39.823
but without having the perception

00:47:39.823 --> 00:47:41.525
their field of individual feeling,

00:47:41.525 --> 00:47:43.026
of affordances

00:47:43.026 --> 00:47:45.863
of this collective audience.

00:47:46.396 --> 00:47:47.130
FRIEDMAN: That's awesome.

00:47:47.130 --> 00:47:49.766
It makes me think of the human capacity

00:47:49.833 --> 00:47:51.602
to have counterfactuals

00:47:51.602 --> 00:47:52.436
and speculative

00:47:52.436 --> 00:47:55.873
realism on teams and projects like, Hey,

00:47:56.373 --> 00:47:59.643
everybody here, we could do X.

00:47:59.643 --> 00:48:01.712
So there's the ability to communicate

00:48:02.045 --> 00:48:04.047
semantically and representational

00:48:04.047 --> 00:48:04.781
anywhere needed

00:48:05.749 --> 00:48:07.618
plausible

00:48:07.618 --> 00:48:10.921
narratives or little sub niches.

00:48:10.921 --> 00:48:14.358
New things can be suggested and arise

00:48:14.358 --> 00:48:15.659
that are specifically

00:48:15.659 --> 00:48:19.796
about shared or collective affordances.

00:48:19.796 --> 00:48:20.898
And then additionally,

00:48:20.898 --> 00:48:24.334
there are special names for when we take

00:48:24.334 --> 00:48:27.070
individual level affordances

00:48:27.604 --> 00:48:29.806
that have consequences

00:48:29.806 --> 00:48:31.742
on other levels of decision

00:48:31.742 --> 00:48:34.011
making, like there might be

00:48:34.011 --> 00:48:36.246
a multisig wallet

00:48:36.513 --> 00:48:37.681
in cryptography

00:48:37.681 --> 00:48:40.150
or a voting system in democracy

00:48:40.150 --> 00:48:42.252
where an individual's affordances

00:48:42.252 --> 00:48:43.820
like to pull the lever

00:48:43.820 --> 00:48:45.289
or to fill in a box

00:48:45.289 --> 00:48:47.658
or to assign a transaction,

00:48:47.658 --> 00:48:49.960
and then it's being engaged in

00:48:51.061 --> 00:48:53.297
specifically because there's knowledge

00:48:53.630 --> 00:48:55.766
if 100 people do this,

00:48:55.766 --> 00:48:57.234
then this performance

00:48:57.234 --> 00:48:58.201
is going to happen.

00:48:58.201 --> 00:49:00.871
So it seems like there's many cases

00:49:00.871 --> 00:49:04.041
where we do

00:49:05.275 --> 00:49:07.277
our mandible closing

00:49:07.277 --> 00:49:10.080
the kind of lower level individual task,

00:49:10.714 --> 00:49:13.250
also with an explicit knowledge

00:49:13.383 --> 00:49:15.752
and a communicated knowledge around

00:49:15.752 --> 00:49:19.022
how someone's individual actions will

00:49:19.323 --> 00:49:20.724
influence group

00:49:21.892 --> 00:49:23.927
outcomes that could be like

00:49:23.927 --> 00:49:25.429
weakly emergent,

00:49:25.429 --> 00:49:26.096
like merely

00:49:26.096 --> 00:49:28.165
submitting the affordances

00:49:28.165 --> 00:49:29.633
taken by individuals

00:49:29.633 --> 00:49:31.401
as well as

00:49:31.401 --> 00:49:32.469
strongly emergent

00:49:32.469 --> 00:49:33.303
or more strongly

00:49:33.303 --> 00:49:34.738
emergent in the sense

00:49:34.738 --> 00:49:36.707
that there's, there's nothing different

00:49:36.707 --> 00:49:38.909
about anyone's pulling lever and voting,

00:49:38.909 --> 00:49:40.811
but there are phase transitions

00:49:40.811 --> 00:49:44.147
and dynamics that can be like top down

00:49:46.083 --> 00:49:49.586
deep.

00:49:49.586 --> 00:49:50.153
TICKLES: Yes.

00:49:50.153 --> 00:49:51.722
So when we have these experiences

00:49:51.722 --> 00:49:52.456
and they are

00:49:52.456 --> 00:49:55.726
kind of absolute in the sense that they

00:49:55.726 --> 00:49:58.362
they've happened, they've occurred and

00:49:59.930 --> 00:50:01.531
whether we can recall them or not,

00:50:01.531 --> 00:50:03.000
they they seem to have

00:50:03.000 --> 00:50:04.601
some kind of an effect

00:50:04.601 --> 00:50:06.837
on this relativity piece and

00:50:06.837 --> 00:50:08.038
and the relationship piece.

00:50:08.038 --> 00:50:10.440
I don't think it matters whether we

00:50:10.440 --> 00:50:13.110
see Newton on one side and then

00:50:13.944 --> 00:50:14.678
Chris Fields

00:50:14.678 --> 00:50:16.380
and an Einstein on the other,

00:50:16.380 --> 00:50:18.448
that the bottom line is, is that to

00:50:18.448 --> 00:50:20.217
what Daniel was just saying,

00:50:20.217 --> 00:50:21.952
the possible happens

00:50:21.952 --> 00:50:22.519
when we

00:50:22.519 --> 00:50:23.553
when we

00:50:23.553 --> 00:50:24.654
don't get stuck on

00:50:24.654 --> 00:50:25.489
what's the gauge

00:50:25.489 --> 00:50:27.124
of the transmission line,

00:50:27.124 --> 00:50:30.427
but what does that now allow us to do?

00:50:30.660 --> 00:50:33.997
So how do we move from the absolutes,

00:50:33.997 --> 00:50:38.368
the modeling piece to the process piece,

00:50:38.802 --> 00:50:40.904
the things that are out there

00:50:40.904 --> 00:50:43.073
that are have not happened yet,

00:50:43.707 --> 00:50:44.408
that are still in

00:50:44.408 --> 00:50:46.910
that possibility category.

00:50:46.910 --> 00:50:49.379
And now we're going to use communication

00:50:49.646 --> 00:50:50.847
not just to narrow

00:50:50.847 --> 00:50:53.350
down to the workbench.

00:50:53.350 --> 00:50:56.253
The ontology, which Daniel and I are

00:50:56.620 --> 00:50:57.921
our fast friends,

00:50:57.921 --> 00:50:58.822
except when it comes

00:50:58.822 --> 00:51:01.124
to the specifics of ontology,

00:51:01.124 --> 00:51:02.659
the generalities of that,

00:51:02.659 --> 00:51:04.561
and the potential impossibility

00:51:04.561 --> 00:51:05.462
of that, really,

00:51:05.462 --> 00:51:07.664
maybe you can talk to us a little bit

00:51:07.664 --> 00:51:10.200
about that from the ecological lens.

00:51:11.768 --> 00:51:14.438
TISON: Yeah, that's a really good question.

00:51:14.438 --> 00:51:16.606
I think the one interesting thing

00:51:17.007 --> 00:51:18.542
about like collective

00:51:18.542 --> 00:51:21.878
and shared affordances is I think they

00:51:22.946 --> 00:51:24.948
they are learned

00:51:24.948 --> 00:51:26.783
in the same way that we learned

00:51:26.783 --> 00:51:28.785
individual affordances.

00:51:28.785 --> 00:51:29.786
So for instance,

00:51:29.786 --> 00:51:31.354
how do we learn how would we

00:51:31.354 --> 00:51:33.557
we we learn to perceive enough audience.

00:51:33.557 --> 00:51:35.392
We learn to perceive in that audience.

00:51:35.392 --> 00:51:37.627
We I think we gain a skill.

00:51:37.828 --> 00:51:38.728
When we gain

00:51:38.728 --> 00:51:39.696
a particular skill,

00:51:39.696 --> 00:51:41.598
we then can perceive in the

00:51:41.598 --> 00:51:43.233
over environment,

00:51:43.233 --> 00:51:44.701
the situations

00:51:44.701 --> 00:51:46.536
where we can apply the skill.

00:51:46.536 --> 00:51:47.904
So for instance,

00:51:47.904 --> 00:51:50.006
when we're really young, we can like

00:51:50.006 --> 00:51:51.842
I guess we can

00:51:52.742 --> 00:51:54.344
then maybe crawl a little bit.

00:51:54.344 --> 00:51:56.446
So we know where surfaces

00:51:56.613 --> 00:51:58.014
can be crawled upon

00:51:58.014 --> 00:51:59.216
and we can grab things.

00:51:59.216 --> 00:51:59.916
So we perceive

00:51:59.916 --> 00:52:01.818
where things can be grabbed.

00:52:01.818 --> 00:52:03.153
And so we start from this

00:52:03.153 --> 00:52:05.155
like basic skills

00:52:05.155 --> 00:52:06.857
and then we explore our environment.

00:52:06.857 --> 00:52:09.559
We do some things that we, we, we're

00:52:09.860 --> 00:52:11.728
gaining some abilities

00:52:11.728 --> 00:52:14.397
and when we do that,

00:52:14.397 --> 00:52:15.932
probably a little bit by trial

00:52:15.932 --> 00:52:16.600
and error,

00:52:16.600 --> 00:52:19.436
we, we begin to perceive some

00:52:19.436 --> 00:52:21.238
higher level affordances can

00:52:21.238 --> 00:52:21.972
because we can do

00:52:21.972 --> 00:52:23.473
some more complex things.

00:52:23.473 --> 00:52:25.742
And so our field of affordances

00:52:25.742 --> 00:52:27.110
deepens and become more

00:52:27.110 --> 00:52:28.345
it becomes more complex

00:52:28.345 --> 00:52:29.913
as our set of skills

00:52:29.913 --> 00:52:31.381
becomes more complex.

00:52:31.381 --> 00:52:33.483
But I think that interacting

00:52:33.483 --> 00:52:35.519
with others, with others

00:52:36.219 --> 00:52:38.955
and so sorry for my, my accent,

00:52:39.055 --> 00:52:39.890
it's not really good.

00:52:39.890 --> 00:52:42.225
I, I didn't want to say interacting with

00:52:42.225 --> 00:52:43.493
the animal others.

00:52:44.895 --> 00:52:46.062
So yes.

00:52:46.062 --> 00:52:47.797
So when we interact with others

00:52:47.797 --> 00:52:49.833
we are also learning

00:52:50.100 --> 00:52:51.835
to do some particular things.

00:52:51.835 --> 00:52:52.936
For instance,

00:52:52.936 --> 00:52:54.504
if I tried to

00:52:54.504 --> 00:52:56.540
to pick something up alone,

00:52:56.540 --> 00:52:58.375
I might not be strong enough to do it.

00:52:58.375 --> 00:53:00.410
So I don't have the skills.

00:53:00.410 --> 00:53:01.878
So I don't perceive that for dense.

00:53:01.878 --> 00:53:03.980
But if in some cases

00:53:03.980 --> 00:53:04.981
I picked something up

00:53:04.981 --> 00:53:06.950
and I see something, somebody else

00:53:06.950 --> 00:53:08.685
picking it up with me

00:53:08.685 --> 00:53:10.887
and we succeed in listing it

00:53:11.087 --> 00:53:13.790
and then I've gained the ability

00:53:13.790 --> 00:53:15.225
to see that

00:53:15.225 --> 00:53:18.161
with somebody else I can lift the stick,

00:53:18.361 --> 00:53:19.596
but it's not a different,

00:53:19.596 --> 00:53:21.331
different kind of learning.

00:53:21.331 --> 00:53:23.633
And in that case,

00:53:23.800 --> 00:53:24.868
from the kind of learning

00:53:24.868 --> 00:53:25.635
that I apply

00:53:25.635 --> 00:53:27.571
when I'm learning individual skills,

00:53:27.571 --> 00:53:29.272
it's just that interacting

00:53:29.272 --> 00:53:30.540
with your environment,

00:53:30.540 --> 00:53:32.209
you acquire skills,

00:53:32.209 --> 00:53:33.777
somebody sometimes with some

00:53:33.777 --> 00:53:35.912
somebody else, sometimes not.

00:53:35.912 --> 00:53:37.047
And you

00:53:37.047 --> 00:53:37.847
understand

00:53:37.847 --> 00:53:39.249
how you can apply these skills

00:53:39.249 --> 00:53:40.483
in your environment

00:53:40.483 --> 00:53:41.851
and then you

00:53:41.851 --> 00:53:43.186
navigate your field

00:53:43.186 --> 00:53:45.155
affordances accordingly.

00:53:45.155 --> 00:53:46.523
So how you perceive

00:53:46.523 --> 00:53:48.291
a possibility is about,

00:53:48.291 --> 00:53:49.226
Oh, you have to learn

00:53:49.226 --> 00:53:51.328
to do some things in the past.

00:53:51.328 --> 00:53:53.163
And then because of this learning,

00:53:53.163 --> 00:53:54.464
you perceive situations

00:53:54.464 --> 00:53:56.733
as affording these of actions.

00:53:56.866 --> 00:53:58.168
